      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T01:52:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah true that it would not integrate well as is. Maybe you can split it into two parts, one clever macro, and one helper function, like:\n\n```cpp\ntemplate \u003ctypename T\u003e\nstd::string MakeIncreaseLimitMessage(std::string_view limitName, T adapterLimitValue) {\n        return absl::StrFormat(\" This adapter supports a higher %s\"\n                               \" of %u, which can be specified in requiredLimits when calling \"   \n                               \"requestDevice(). Limits differ by hardware, so always check the \" \n                               \"adapter limits prior to requesting a higher limit.\",              \n                               limitName, adapterLimitValue);                                   \n\n}\n\n#define DAWN_INCREASE_LIMIT_MESSAGE(adapter, limitName, limitValue)                               \\\n    [\u0026]() -\u003e std::string {                                                                        \\\n        SupportedLimits adapterLimits;                                                            \\\n        wgpu::Status status \u003d adapter-\u003eAPIGetLimits(\u0026adapterLimits);                              \\\n        DAWN_ASSERT(status \u003d\u003d wgpu::Status::Success);                                             \\\n        if (limitValue \u003e adapterLimits.limits.limitName) {                                        \\\n            return \"\";                                                                            \\\n        }                                                                                         \\\n        return MakeIncreaseLimitMessage(#limitName, adapterLimits.limit.limitName);               \\\n    }()\n```",
      "parentUuid": "242d696a_be5b7b86",
